  "details": "<p>This archive is located in the\u00a0South-West Palace<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-0c1c18ae-7fff-5320-6d88-0d39b5a48d5d\">.\u00a0<span>Exact findspots do not exist for tablets from the nineteenth century excavations.</span></span></p>\r\n<p><span>\u00a0</span><img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"531\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/Plan75_Kuyunjik_Nineveh1-5_p160.png\" width=\"462\" /></p>\r\n<p><img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"537\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/Plan76_southwest_palace_Nineveh1-3_p162.png\" width=\"471\" /></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "In the Palace of Sennacherib (South-West Palace) at Nineveh, in Room LIV, nineteenth-century British excavators found the remains of an archive consisting of cuneiform tablets, some of which also included summary notes in Aramaic.",
